           \n          \n        \n          </a>\n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  <a href=\"https://keningzhu.notion.site/sharing-space-camp-orientation-preview-11-min-2530906669588096a0eae886bcc1a80b?source=copy_link\" target=\"_blank\">\n    watch the orientation video\n  </a>\n\n<hr /> \n\n\n  <p>this month I emerged from the all-consuming process that was teaching the live session of <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/sharing-space-camp\">sharing space camp</a> — which, I think was my best teaching work yet. I’m currently transitioning the course to a self-paced, asynchronous experience. </p><p>I’ve decided to excerpt the first 11 minutes of the welcome/orientation video that I made for the course, to share with you here. </p><p><strong>in this video, I’ll explore</strong></p><ul><li><p>why space camp as conceptual container </p></li><li><p>why I’m teaching this course</p></li><li><p>bridging art + business through the internet </p></li><li><p>space camp container, journey, itinerary</p></li><li><p>seasonality in learning experiences </p></li><li><p>my teaching methodology: fractal + cyclical   </p></li><li><p>the winding journey through the dark </p></li><li><p>transforming the “task/challenge” of sharing your work. </p></li></ul><p></p><blockquote><h2><em>“Our challenge is to change the question. Not \"How do I reach people?\" but </em><strong><em>\"How do I be so in my creative power and flow that I can trust that the right people will come to me?\"</em></strong></h2></blockquote><p></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <p>📺 <a href=\"https://keningzhu.notion.site/sharing-space-camp-orientation-preview-11-min-2530906669588096a0eae886bcc1a80b?source=copy_link\" target=\"_blank\">watch the 11 minute orientation video</a><br />🚀 explore <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/sharing-space-camp\">sharing space camp</a></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\